<h2>News &amp; updates</h2>
<p class="updated">Last updated September 9, 2026</p>
<!-- NEW-ARTICLES-HERE -->

<div class="news-item">
  <div class="date">September 8, 2026</div>
  <h3>Fines begin: DSNY starts ticketing buildings without official NYC Bins</h3>
  <p>The warning period ended on Labor Day. DSNY is now issuing summonses starting at $50 to properties with 1-9 residential units that set out trash in anything other than an official NYC Bin. The city says trash bins are in stock at every Home Depot in the five boroughs.</p>
  <div class="src"><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/dsny/news/26-035/starting-sept-8-residential-properties-1-9-units-must-use-official-nyc-bins-face-50">DSNY Press Release #26-035 (Aug 26)</a> &middot; <a href="https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2026/09/08/city-will-now-issue-fines-for-small-buildings-not-using-official-trash-bins">NY1</a></div>
</div>

<div class="news-item">
  <div class="date">September 7, 2026</div>
  <h3>Gothamist: ~750,000 small buildings face the new fines</h3>
  <p>Gothamist's enforcement-eve report: fines run $50 to $200 for repeat offenders; roughly 750,000 buildings are covered; and Council members say constituents struggled to find bins during the summer supply crunch. DSNY says the bins remain available for sale.</p>
  <div class="src"><a href="https://gothamist.com/news/owners-of-small-nyc-buildings-face-fines-for-failure-to-use-official-trash-bins">Gothamist</a></div>
</div>

<div class="news-item">
  <div class="date">August 5, 2026</div>
  <h3>NYC Bin manufacturer Otto in involuntary bankruptcy</h3>
  <p>Waste Dive reports Otto Environmental Systems - holder of the city's bin contract - was placed in involuntary Chapter 7 bankruptcy in May by three creditors alleging $2.6M in debts. Court filings describe disputes over assets moved between companies set up by Otto's CEO. About 1.1 million NYC Bins have been purchased; the city had expected 3.39 million delivered by May 2026. Home Depot listings now carry the official bin under the Edge brand, and DSNY maintains supply is stable.</p>
  <div class="src"><a href="https://www.wastedive.com/news/otto-environmental-systems-involuntary-bankruptcy-nyc-bins-contract/827070/">Waste Dive</a></div>
</div>

<div class="news-item">
  <div class="date">May 2026</div>
  <h3>Reimbursement window for STAR homeowners closes with the warning period</h3>
  <p>Owners of one- and two-family homes who received the STAR exemption or credit in 2024 or 2025 were eligible for a reimbursement covering one 45-gallon bin. The deadline was extended through the first week of September 2026 and has now closed.</p>
  <div class="src"><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/dsny/collection/containerization/nyc-bins.page">DSNY NYC Bins</a></div>
</div>

<div class="news-item">
  <div class="date">June 1, 2026</div>
  <h3>Official NYC Bins become mandatory for trash at 1-9 unit buildings</h3>
  <p>The containerization program's next phase took effect: only official NYC Bins count for trash setout. A summer warning period ran through Labor Day while bin supply recovered from the manufacturer's troubles.</p>
  <div class="src"><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/dsny/collection/containerization/residential-containerization.page">DSNY Residential Containerization</a></div>
</div>
